WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.734
Aladdin left the palace with his head hanging down.

2
00:00:04.735 --> 00:00:08.982
Feeling hopeless, he walked through the city gate.

3
00:00:08.983 --> 00:00:13.548
The land was wide open outside the city walls.

4
00:00:13.549 --> 00:00:19.310
Soon Aladdin came to a swift river and sat down.

5
00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:24.720
"Oh, Princess, how will I ever find you?" Aladdin wondered.

6
00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:26.995
"Will I ever see you again?"

7
00:00:26.996 --> 00:00:29.843
He stared at the rippling water.

8
00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:33.375
"I should just throw myself into this river."

9
00:00:33.376 --> 00:00:36.664
He put his face in his hands and wept.

10
00:00:36.665 --> 00:00:43.138
When he finally wiped the tears away, he noticed something on one of his fingers.

11
00:00:43.139 --> 00:00:48.307
"Magrib’s ring!" cried Aladdin. "The little genie!"

12
00:00:48.308 --> 00:00:52.966
He rubbed the ring until a cloud of bright smoke appeared.

13
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:59.789
"The genie of the ring has come!" squeaked the little man with bells on his cap.

14
00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.560
"What’s the problem?"

15
00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:07.943
"Oh, genie," said Aladdin, "bring back my palace and my wife!"

16
00:01:07.944 --> 00:01:11.076
"Your wish is my command, master!"

17
00:01:11.077 --> 00:01:14.744
said the little genie as he raised his arms.

18
00:01:14.745 --> 00:01:16.691
Then he stopped.

19
00:01:16.692 --> 00:01:21.075
"Did you ask me to bring back your palace and your wife?"

20
00:01:21.076 --> 00:01:24.016
"Yes, I did," Aladdin answered.

21
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:27.701
"Well, I’ve got bad news," said the genie of the ring.

22
00:01:27.702 --> 00:01:30.130
"I can’t do it.

23
00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:34.290
The genie of the lamp’s magic took your palace and your wife.

24
00:01:34.291 --> 00:01:37.074
Where is the lamp?"

25
00:01:37.075 --> 00:01:41.511
"I don’t know," said Aladdin, feeling sad again.

26
00:01:41.512 --> 00:01:47.058
"Sorry, I cannot undo another genie’s magic," replied the genie.

27
00:01:47.059 --> 00:01:50.053
"Those are the rules."

28
00:01:50.054 --> 00:01:53.501
"Wait, can you take me to the princess?"

29
00:01:53.502 --> 00:02:00.941
"Of course!" said the genie. "Let’s go!"

30
00:02:00.942 --> 00:02:05.432
When Aladdin found himself outside his palace, it was night.

31
00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:08.239
His home was dark and quiet.

32
00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.359
"I’ll wait until morning," Aladdin told himself.

33
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:18.148
He lay down under Princess Badra’s window and fell asleep.

34
00:02:18.149 --> 00:02:23.155
The next morning, the princess was sitting in her room with her attendants.

35
00:02:23.156 --> 00:02:27.430
From time to time, she sighed and wiped away a tear.

36
00:02:27.431 --> 00:02:31.948
"This is such a strange place," she cried.

37
00:02:31.949 --> 00:02:35.681
"And where is my Aladdin?"

38
00:02:35.682 --> 00:02:39.354
"Maybe some fresh air will bring color to your cheeks,"

39
00:02:39.355 --> 00:02:43.121
said one attendant as she opened a window.

40
00:02:43.122 --> 00:02:48.349
"Nothing will help me feel better," said the princess sadly.

41
00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.212
"Princess!" shouted the woman at the window.

42
00:02:52.213 --> 00:02:56.967
"Look! I see Aladdin asleep under the window!"

43
00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.724
Princess Badra ran over to look.

44
00:02:59.725 --> 00:03:04.925
"Aladdin!" she called out. "My dear husband!"

45
00:03:04.926 --> 00:03:11.936
Aladdin’s eyes quickly opened, and he looked up to see his wife’s beautiful face.

46
00:03:11.937 --> 00:03:16.620
"Run and open the door!" said the princess to a servant.

47
00:03:16.621 --> 00:03:22.439
Within moments, Aladdin was racing up the steps toward the princess’s room.

48
00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:28.219
But instead of embracing her, he ran straight into his bedroom.

49
00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.850
"My lamp!" he cried as he rushed back to the princess.

50
00:03:31.851 --> 00:03:34.057
"Where is my lamp?"

51
00:03:34.058 --> 00:03:37.557
"It is gone," said the princess.

52
00:03:37.558 --> 00:03:40.443
"I traded it to an old man for a new lamp.

53
00:03:40.444 --> 00:03:45.004
Then all of a sudden, I ended up in Egypt."

54
00:03:45.005 --> 00:03:49.853
"Egypt!" said Aladdin. "Magrib must have done this!"

55
00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:52.907
Aladdin described the magician to his wife.

56
00:03:52.908 --> 00:03:54.973
"Was he the old man?"

57
00:03:54.974 --> 00:03:58.720
"Yes, husband," the princess replied.

58
00:03:58.721 --> 00:04:02.956
"I don’t like him. He smells funny."

59
00:04:02.957 --> 00:04:07.166
"Where does Magrib keep the lamp?" Aladdin asked.

60
00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:11.000
"He carries it in his coat," said the princess.

61
00:04:11.001 --> 00:04:15.499
"He shows it to me and smiles strangely when he visits."

62
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.388
"He visits you?" said Aladdin.

63
00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:22.740
"Yes," answered the princess.

64
00:04:22.741 --> 00:04:26.371
"He comes every day and asks me to marry him.

65
00:04:26.372 --> 00:04:30.974
He told me you were dead, but I didn’t believe him."

66
00:04:30.975 --> 00:04:33.409
Aladdin thought a moment.

67
00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:40.420
Then he told Princess Badra what she had to do.

